&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercially minded, hands-on Senior Human Resources Manager to lead all People &amp;amp; Culture functions at our Australian fulfillment center. Serving as the dedicated HR Business Partner to the Site Director, you will own the end-to-end people strategy, workforce capability, and daily HR operations for a large, multi-shift frontline and salaried workforce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating within a matrixed People model, you will manage an on-site HR team while partnering closely with our specialised Centres of Excellence (COEs)—including Talent Acquisition, Total Rewards, People Operations, and Work Health &amp;amp; Safety (WHS)—to translate people initiatives into practical, high-impact site execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Business Partnering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Site Leadership Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a trusted advisor and coach to the Site Director and site department heads on organisational design, leadership effectiveness, change management, and peak-volume workforce scaling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workforce Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Site Operations, Planning, and Workforce Staffing to forecast seasonal headcount requirements, optimise labour mix (permanent vs. casual/agency), and align staffing plans with production targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local Organizational Design &amp;amp; Effectiveness&lt;/strong&gt;: Act as a thought partner and provide strategic influence to the Site Operations team when it comes to performance management, team structuring, succession planning, and ensuring team members fully understand their job expectations and accountability measures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Site HR Operations &amp;amp; Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
